KZ3 patch 2209 (RSX pass 174): RSX_WALK_TRIVIAL=1, the trivial-walker measurement switch (default off, diagnostic, never shipped).

The walker still consumes the FIFO and keeps labels, semaphores, reports and guest copies in order (cellGcmSys.c untouched in behaviour),
but the live-draw sink drops every begin / draw / inline array / indexed draw / end / clear (counted) and a flip is consumed without
presenting. Prints [walk-trivial] once at arm (naming what happens to the guest write-backs: GPU-output write-backs surf_wb, wbd_drain,
report_rb never run because no surface or query exists; render-target guest bytes stay as last written, NOT zero-filled) and once per
second (flips, methods, dropped draws/clears, released labels/reports, guest copies, GPU write-backs run (expected 0) and requests seen).
Pure core libs/video/rsx_walk_trivial.h, host test tools/smoke/test_walk_trivial.sh. Purpose: main-thread compute and SPU floors without
the walker (U1/U2). NOT run in the game.

